{"id": 19, "ts": 1780583058.49377, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s focus on decision\u2011making and stress resilience. Those are indeed core safety criteria for long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fC demonstrates clear strengths here: he \u201cmakes correct decisions quickly,\u201d has \u201cexcellent attention skills,\u201d is noted as 100\u202f% reliable, and \u201ccreates a positive crew atmosphere\u201d while putting concern for others above everything. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while conscientious and good under stress, has a documented weakness in attention \u2013 James noted a \u201cweak memory for numbers\u201d \u2013 and we have no evidence of his decision\u2011quality in safety\u2011critical situations (Sarah reported none). Given that precise calculations and rapid, correct decisions are non\u2011negotiable for this role, the balance of evidence now favors Candidate\u202fC despite his communication and egocentric concerns, which can be addressed through crew\u2011resource\u2011management training. Therefore, I shift my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC."}
